---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `I am driving to my cousin's this weekend and I want to know
what the gas is going to run me before I commit. My car is
pretty good on gas but I do not remember the exact number,
so I would rather type it in each time than have it built in.`;

const SampleOutput = `How far are you driving (miles)? 420
What is your car's mpg? 32
Price per gallon? 3.49

Gallons needed: 13.125
Trip cost: 45.80625`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-1" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 1
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Trip Cost</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-1">Set 1</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Three things have to come from the person running the program, not from you.</li>
            <li>Gas is sold by the gallon and the car is measured in miles per gallon. Work out how many gallons the trip needs before you work out the money.</li>
            <li>Money looks wrong with five decimal places. You do not have the tool to fix that until Activity 1.8 &mdash; if it bothers you, come back after it.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="where-to-start">
          <h2>Where to Start</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Only one-star challenges have this section.</b> If you already know how to
            begin, skip it &mdash; and when you move up to two stars, working out the order
            yourself is part of the job.
          </p>

          <ol>
            <li>Three prompts, three casts.</li>
            <li>Work out the gallons needed before you work out the cost.</li>
            <li>Then multiply by the price.</li>
            <li>Print both numbers, not just the total. Seeing the gallons makes a wrong answer easier to spot.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={SampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">45.80625 is the honest answer. Activity 1.8 shows how to display it as 45.81.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-trip-cost</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
